iving with named  andrew loaned me his dive light and it  made a huge difference i could kind of  see the pike reflecting gold in the  light and there was about four pike in  this little cove that i saw and one of  them i actually got to spear  unfortunately  my gopro battery died and i didn't get  it on camera  okay i have no idea how much my head cam  was recording because it died right out  there but we just saw one jump and went  in there and just tried to check it  around saw four really quick using a  dive light and i tagged one that came  off the spear  and then these guys  found him  just hanging out on the surface so  so maybe i got an assist  there you go  that's a really a pretty typical sized  pike around here i imagine right yeah  they got tons of teeth on them they'll  chew your fingers up so bad oh yeah look  at those tiny little chompers oh it's  like a stick your finger  pad in there  you woke him up  alex those are yours oh sweet  look at that  well there we go guys that was some  rough visibility but that was loads of  fun  so in the end i think only three fish  got tagged but uh  you know it was a good time but i need  to clean up my fish and get that gutted  before i run out of light all right guys  i'm back at the house and we're gonna  cook up one of those pike we were gonna  donate them but because we shot so few  of them uh we decided not to waste the  hospital's time and uh we're just gonna  cook them up so i've got one of them and  i'm gonna cook it up and i'm gonna try  some funky recipes because we are  leaving on a plane tonight and i didn't  have time to go out and do a bunch of  shopping and fancy cooking so we're  gonna do kind of uh  what do we have in the cupboard sort of  cooking thing and i got some fun ideas  if you think that freshwater fish  sometimes tastes a little bit muddy add  buttermilk or vinegar to the meat and  let it sit for just anywhere from 40  minutes to a few hours and just let it  marinate in that just a little